<title>Introduction to Data Manager</title>

<b>Data Manager</b> is a tool that allows you to <link views.csdoc>examine</link>, <link menu_summary.csdoc>modify</link>, and <link downloading_and_synchronizing_data.csdoc>synchronize</link> cases in a CSPro <link CSPro::data_sources.csdoc>data source</link>. Once a data source is open in Data Manager, it can be used seamlessly, without having to respecify dictionary or data sources (such as when invoking the <link CSExport::introduction_to_export_data.csdoc>Export Data</link> or <link CSFreq::introduction_to_tabulate_frequencies.csdoc>Tabulate Frequencies</link> tools).

This guide contains the following information:

